<article class="env-definition" id="016Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/016Z">Definition <span data-tag="016Z">14.9.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $U$ and $V$ be cosimplicial objects of $\mathcal{C}$. Assume the products $U_ n \times V_ n$ exist in $\mathcal{C}$. The <em>product of $U$ and $V$</em> is the cosimplicial object $U \times V$ defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$(U \times V)_ n = U_ n \times V_ n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any $\varphi : [n] \to [m]$ the map $(U \times V)(\varphi ) : U_ n \times V_ n \to U_ m \times V_ m$ is the product $U(\varphi ) \times V(\varphi )$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>